assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2021-02-15T00:28:00Z","updated_at":"2024-03-15T14:29:05Z","closed_at":"2024-03-15T14:29:05Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"#### Problem Description\r\n![Screenshot](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/9620335/107893232-e4503e00-6f21-11eb-862c-ae6e8746d79e.png)\r\n\r\nAs shown in the screenshot above, the overflowed part of the view options menu doesn't get displayed if the flow detail section is too short.\r\n\r\nRemoving the `overflow` property on `.flow-detail` and the `overflow-y` property on `.flow-detail section` fixes the issue, but will conflict with the fix of issue #2083. Maybe find a different solution for that issue, or set the `overflow` property of `dropdown-menu` to `auto` and limit the height of it by set its `top` property to a fixed value, like `-300px`.\r\n\r\n#### Steps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n1. Open a flow detail that is short enough\r\n2. Open the view options menu\r\n3. The menu get displayed as shown in the screenshot above\r\n\r\n#### System Information\r\nMitmproxy: 6.0.2\r\nPython: 3.9.1\r\nOpenSSL: OpenSSL 1.1.1i  8 Dec 2020\r\nPlatform: Windows-10-10.0.16299-SP0\r\nFirefox: 86.0b9","closed_by":{"login":"mhils","id":1019198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTkxOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1019198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils","html_url":"https://github.com/mhils","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhils/